  "_": "Z373 the Meshy community models for the battlefields (tools/scene-import.mjs). src: a file in ~/Downloads (substring of its name); tris: the near (desktop, up close) triangle budget, 0 = every triangle of the scan; tex: its texture size. From it the tool also builds the mid copy (l/: 18 %, 1K maps) and the far copy (f/: 3 %, 512 maps) — Z392 a share of lodBase when the near copy is heavier (the near scan stays whole for up close; the copies seen from 24 m on stay light) for the distance levels, and m: the phone copy's budget (1K maps). Z387 out / file: a hand weapon — one plain file (no distance copies) at assets/models/real/<out>/<file>.glb, turned rot° about Y so its barrel lies along Z. loose: foliage — the lighter copies may simplify across texture seams (alpha-cut leaf cards: a smeared leaf far off is still green). err: the near (or only) copy's simplification error. Z424 looseNear / looseMid / looseFar are gone: collapsing a hard surface across its seams shattered its texture into confetti (Z420, 60 models); a copy whose seams hold it far above its budget now gets its maps baked anew (tools/scene-bake.mjs). hd {key, px}: such a baked copy's sharp near maps too (assets/models/real/hd/<key>.0.map|nrm.webp — tools/hd-maps.mjs cannot cut them from the original once the copy has its own atlas). Z425 cut: the lowest share of the scan's height dropped before anything else (a round photographed standing in a stump); rebake: its lighter copies (l, f, m) baked anew even when their seams hold them in budget (a thin rim crumples when thinned seam-locked).",
